{"duration_api_ms":1634918,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8ab6682a-3eba-4ac5-96e7-fb459630bd7b","total_cost_usd":48.877318500000015,"usage":{"input_tokens":208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":259285,"cache_read_input_tokens":50356168,"output_tokens":87436,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":33272},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":259285,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4539,"cache_read_input_tokens":630048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":449},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":412,"outputTokens":164735,"thinkingTokens":52590,"cacheReadInputTokens":76903827,"cacheCreationInputTokens":630497,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":48.877318500000015,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":105,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All seven route picks (R1–R7) are implemented. `dart analyze lib test` now exits 0 and `flutter test` passes 50/50, including 6 new FLV tests. None of the native, platform or CI changes were built or run (Linux, macOS, iOS, the Windows C++ from iter 1, the workflows). I also didn't run the app, so every UI change is unverified on a device.\n\n## 1. What changed, per item\n\n**R1 — deleting a download vs. the exported folder**\n- New `showDeleteDownloadDialog` (`lib/pages/download/delete_dialog.dart`) shows a checkbox \"同时删除导出的视频文件\", **unchecked by default**. It returns null when cancelled, otherwise whether to delete the export.\n- `deleteDownload` and `deletePage` take `deleteExported` (default false). The exported folder is deleted only when it is true.\n- Every delete entry point uses the new dialog:\n  - long-press on an item (`DetailItem`, used by the downloads, detail, downloading and search pages)\n  - long-press on a multi-part page\n  - multi-select on the downloads, detail and search pages\n- The downloading queue has no exported file yet, so its dialog shows no checkbox. Its multi-select still uses the old confirm dialog.\n\n**R2 — self-test isolation**\n- `isSelfTestProfile` is set from `--selftest` before any storage init.\n- App data (Hive boxes, WebView data) then lives in `<appSupport>/selftest`. Downloads use the default download folder inside it; the user's custom download path and Android external storage are ignored.\n- The Android public `Download/LibrePili` export is skipped too.\n- The self-test's clean-up deletes, which now pass `deleteExported: true`, can therefore only touch the isolated folders.\n- The report now records `dataDir` and `downloadDir`.\n\n**R3 — old single-URL (Type1) downloads**\n- Every `durl` segment is now downloaded, not just the first. Each segment has its backup URLs, the segments run one after another as `0.mp4`, `1.mp4`, …, and progress is shown over their total size.\n- New pure-Dart FLV demuxer `lib/utils/flv_demux.dart`, a `part` of `mp4_remux.dart`, so it reuses the existing mp4 writer:\n  - H.264 video and AAC audio.\n  - It reads `avcC` and the AudioSpecificConfig from the sequence-header tags, and parses the SPS for the picture size, including cropping.\n  - It keeps composition time offsets and keyframe flags.\n  - Segments whose timestamps restart are placed after the previous one.\n  - If audio and video start at different times, an empty edit keeps them in sync.\n  - Sample bytes are copied unchanged (a chunk can now come from its own segment file).\n- Merge rules:\n  - FLV → remux to a real mp4.\n  - Unsupported codec → the original data is kept under its real extension (`<base>.flv`, or `<base>.2.flv` and so on for more segments), and the Android media scan is told `video/x-flv`.\n  - A single mp4 segment is moved as before.\n\n**R4 — offline comments and images**\n- Comment pictures and the emotes used in comment text are downloaded with the comments into `comments_images/`, one file per URL hash.\n- The comments JSON records `pictures` and `emotes` as paths relative to the comments file. This follows the existing comment-count settings; there is no separate toggle.\n- `LocalReplyPanel` shows a local placeholder instead of the avatar, draws emotes inline and pictures as thumbnails (tap to enlarge), all from local files. The panel no longer makes any network request.\n\n**R5 — hide-interaction scope**\nNew shared gate `LoginPolicy.canInteract`: logged in and the switch off. Comments and danmaku still display everywhere; only writing UI is hidden. Entry points gated this pass:\n1. Dynamic, article/opus, music and match detail: the \"评论\" floating button (`common_dyn_page.dart` `replyButton`).\n2. Comment page (`MainReplyPage`, also used by audio): the floating button.\n3. PGC reviews: the \"写短评 / 写长评\" button.\n4. Live room input bar: the \"发送弹幕\" tap and the emoji button. The danmaku toggle and like button stay.\n5. Live room player bar \"发弹幕\" (it was login-only before).\n6. Live chat long-press \"@TA\".\n7. `LiveRoomController.onSendDanmaku` returns early (covers any other path).\n8. `VideoDetailController.showShootDanmakuSheet` returns early (covers the player's keyboard shortcut).\n9. `ReplyController.onReply` and `VideoReplyReplyController.onReply` return early, as a backstop for every comment and reply opener.\n\nAlready gated before this pass, and checked: the video-page comment button, the reply button on each comment item, and the video page's \"发弹幕\" in portrait and fullscreen. A search for the three write APIs (`replyAdd`, `shootDanmaku`, `sendLiveMsg`) found only the three writer pages, and every path into them is now gated. The setting's subtitle now says it applies app-wide.\n\n**R6 — iOS/macOS/Linux identifiers** (matching Android's `com.zxa24.librepili` and Windows' `LibrePili`)\n- Linux: `APPLICATION_ID` is `com.zxa24.librepili` and the binary is `librepili`; the window title reads \"LibrePili\".\n- The desktop file is renamed to `com.zxa24.librepili.desktop`.\n- Debian package metadata is updated: the package name, install paths, and the purge path. Homepage now points to the fork repo.\n- The Linux CI workflow builds tar/deb/rpm/AppImage packages named `LibrePili_linux_*`.\n- macOS: product name `LibrePili`, bundle id `com.zxa24.librepili`, `LibrePili.app` in the Xcode project and scheme, and a `LibrePili_macos_*.dmg` artifact.\n- iOS: bundle id `com.zxa24.librepili`, display and bundle name `LibrePili`, and a `LibrePili_ios_*.ipa` artifact.\n- Signing and secrets are untouched.\n\n**R7 — analyzer warnings**\n- Removed the 5 unused imports.\n- Removed the imports my own edits made unused, including `accounts.dart` in the live header control.\n\n## 2. Diff\n\n`git diff --stat` (cumulative, iter 1 plus this pass): **63 files, +1269 / −510**. The iter-1 hunks are unchanged from my first report.\n\nNew untracked files (not in `git diff`):\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/utils/flv_demux.dart` (FLV demuxer, `part of mp4_remux.dart`) | 533 |\n| `lib/pages/download/delete_dialog.dart` | 46 |\n| `assets/linux/com.zxa24.librepili.desktop` (replaces the deleted `com.example.piliplus.desktop`) | 11 |\n| `test/utils/flv_demux_test.dart` (test/ is gitignored and needs force-adding) | 293 |\n\nModified files this pass:\n- **Linux, CI, iOS, macOS:** `linux_x64.yml`, `mac.yml`, `ios.yml`, `assets/linux/DEBIAN/*`, `linux/CMakeLists.txt`, `linux/runner/my_application.cc`, `ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`, `ios/Runner/Info.plist`, `macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`, `macos/Runner.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/xcschemes/Runner.xcscheme`, `macos/Runner/Configs/AppInfo.xcconfig`\n- **R1 (delete dialog):** `lib/pages/download/{controller,view}.dart`, `lib/pages/download/detail/view.dart`, `lib/pages/download/detail/widgets/item.dart`, `lib/pages/download/downloading/view.dart`, `lib/pages/download/search/{controller,view}.dart`\n- **R2 (self-test profile):** `lib/main.dart`, `lib/utils/path_utils.dart`, `lib/utils/self_test.dart`\n- **R3 (Type1/FLV):** `lib/http/download.dart`, `lib/utils/mp4_remux.dart`\n- **R4 (offline comments):** `lib/services/download/download_extras.dart`, `lib/pages/video/reply/local_reply_panel.dart`\n- **R5 (interaction gate):** `lib/utils/accounts/login_policy.dart`, `lib/pages/common/dyn/common_dyn_page.dart`, `lib/pages/common/reply_controller.dart`, `lib/pages/video/reply_reply/controller.dart`, `lib/pages/main_reply/view.dart`, `lib/pages/pgc_review/view.dart`, `lib/pages/live_room/{controller,view}.dart`, `lib/pages/live_room/widgets/{chat_panel,header_control}.dart`, `lib/pages/video/controller.dart`, `lib/pages/setting/models/extra_settings.dart`\n- **R7 (imports):** `lib/http/live.dart`, `lib/http/video.dart`, `lib/pages/audio/view.dart`, `lib/pages/mine/controller.dart`\n- **`lib/services/download/download_service.dart`** (R1 + R2 + R3): `deleteExported` on both delete methods, the Android export skipped for the self-test profile, the segment chain `_startSegment`, collecting the segment files for the merge, `_exportType1`, and the MIME type passed to `_scanMedia`.\n\n## 3. Uncertainty list\n\n- **R1**\n  - If an entry is deleted *while it is merging*, its just-written output is still always removed (iter-1 behaviour), because the user never saw an export to keep.\n  - The downloading queue's multi-select keeps the plain confirm dialog; nothing there has an export.\n- **R2**\n  - The isolated profile has no accounts or settings, so the self-test always runs anonymous with default settings. Any scenario that relied on the real profile (a login or custom settings) will behave differently.\n  - The image cache in the shared temp folder is not isolated. It is a cache, not user data.\n- **R3**\n  - **Not tested on a real FLV from Bilibili.** Only synthetic FLVs were tested.\n  - Resuming a finished segment relies on the server answering the `Range` request with a 416 that carries `Content-Range: bytes */N`. Without that header, the segment is downloaded again (slower but correct).\n  - Multi-segment mp4 (not FLV) is kept as separate `.mp4` parts. The remuxer can't join progressive mp4 files.\n  - A codec configuration that changes mid-stream is treated as unsupported, so the FLV is kept as is.\n  - An in-app player fallback (merge failed) still plays only segment 0, as before.\n- **R4**\n  - Images come over the network at download time through `Request.dio`, not bound to any account.\n  - A picture that fails to download is simply left out.\n  - Images are downloaded one by one, so a download with many images makes comment export slower; it no longer blocks the queue (iter 1).\n- **R5**\n  - I searched for the three write APIs and all their callers. Writing features outside comments, danmaku and live chat are not gated: private messages, reposting a dynamic with text, creating dynamics.\n  - The live-room gate uses `LoginPolicy.canInteract`, i.e. `Accounts.main.isLogin`, while the input bar itself still checks `LiveRoomController.isLogin` first.\n- **R6**\n  - Changing the Linux application id and the macOS/iOS bundle id moves those platforms' data folders. Anyone who already ran a LibrePili build on those platforms under the old ids starts with an empty profile.\n  - The Android Java/Kotlin package (`com.example.piliplus`) and the audio notification channel id were left alone. This matches Android's current setup, where only `applicationId` changed.\n  - Settings export and WebDAV file names (`piliplus_*`) are unchanged.\n\n## 4. Test results\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: dart analyze + flutter test\n  command: source \".../local_env.sh\" && cd \"$REPO\" && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 50\n  passed: 50\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: 40000\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` exited 0 with no errors or warnings (36 infos). The first test run caught a real bug in my segment joining: the restart threshold was larger than a short segment. I fixed it (a 100 ms tolerance) before the final run.\n\nTwo MCP notes: Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and the agentbridge server failed to connect. Neither was needed here.","ttft_ms":4008,"type":"result","duration_ms":1241454,"uuid":"538ca7c7-f2bb-41ab-9ddd-9cae74e36115","ttft_stream_ms":3580,"time_to_request_ms":899,"first_content_frame_ms":3581,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":1}
